From d80bcabbaa706bd1cef90d7ee6cec1ad3c562df5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 09:34:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] BUDGET-PROBE-1: model health probes with a real token budget
 (qnfo-ai-calibration 1.6.0-budget-probe-1)

Root cause: ai_model_health.status = 'ok' was written by two probes that never read
a reply a caller would get. The folded prober's probeOne sends max_tokens 1 and
returns ok on any non-throwing call; the sweep's probeCompletion sends max_tokens 16
and accepts reasoning_content as an answer. A reasoning model that spends its token
budget thinking and returns empty content (finish_reason length) therefore read ok:
on 2026-10-19 glm-5.3-flash (0.527 error share over 6,065 calls) and qwen3.8-27b
(0.769 over 108) were both ok, so the model router and the code-loop ladder kept
choosing rungs that answer nothing.

Change (worker, minor: it changes what ok means):
- judgeBudgetReply / replyParts / probeBudgetCompletion: one request shaped like a
  caller's (a one-line sum, max_tokens 256, a DONE marker). Empty content or no
  marker is a failed probe.
- Sweep: a model that passes the cheap ping gets one budget probe (not hedged, a
  reply from another model is inconclusive); a failure takes the existing
  degraded -> failing path at fail_threshold and files the existing
  [ai-cal] model probe failing issue. Result rows probe=model-budget.
- Prober member 2.3.16: probeOne is kept verbatim (prober-fold.test.mjs pins it line
  for line); applyBudgetProbe runs right after it, text models only, once per unique
  model id per run, and flips the result to a failed probe, which runProbe already
  writes as degraded -> failing. No new status value, latency semantics unchanged.
- ai_calibration_config budget_probe = off reverts both writers to the ping-only
  verdict without a deploy. A breached ai_spend cap never skips the probe
  (BUDGET-SOFT-ROUTE-1): it is already the lean shape.
- ai-health-prober is FOLDED and not touched.

Migration 2026-10-19-model-health-budget-probe.sql: budget_probe config row, its
control_registry kill-switch row, failure mode health-ok-but-empty with the
fm-health-ok-but-empty detector contract (reads 2 today on live D1), a decision_log
row, and the cost per day (about 144 probe calls, at most about 5,500 neurons).

Tests: qnfo-ai-calibration/budget-probe.test.mjs (45 checks; 20 fail on the base
commit, 0 fail now). prober-fold.test.mjs no longer pins the member version
exactly (asserts a minimum) and tells a member budget row from a calibration run.

Not in this change: the paired A/B harness for answer quality (2828, qnfo-model-eval)
and the rows of models outside both rosters (gemma, llama, qwen3-30b, nemotron-3-120b),
which no probe in this worker covers.

Issues: agent_issues 2829 (path A; the GitHub numbers 1777 and 1778 in the cluster are closed unrelated rows). Pillar: cost.

